    <h2>Chapter 1</h2>
    <p>
        Molly had been staring out of <b>her window</b> for about an hour now.<br>
        On her desk, lying between the copies of <i>Nature</i>, <i>New Scientist</i>, and other scientific journals, was a well-thumbed copy of <cite>On The Road</cite>. It had been Molly's favorite book since college.
    </p>
    <hr>
    <p>
        She had spent the last ten years in this room, sitting under a poster with an Oscar Wilde quote:
        <q>Work is the refuge of people who have nothing better to do</q>.
        Her work on llama <abbr title="Deoxyribonucleic acid">DNA</abbr> was an outstanding achievement, but Molly <em>did</em> think she had something better to do.
    </p>
